1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,120
<i>Previously, on the night shift...</i>

2
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,900
[RAIN DRUMMING ON GLASS]

3
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:17,600
MARCUS: You're late again, Elena.

4
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:20,050
- I know.
- That's not an answer.

5
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:23,400
I said I'd cover for you once,
and I meant once.

6
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:24,300
Fine.

7
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:28,900
Look, the bus never came, my phone died,
and I ran eleven blocks in the rain.

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,100
Right.

9
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:34,200
ELENA: Are you kidding me? You think
I wanted to spend my morning like that?

10
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:36,000
{\an8}ST. AUGUSTINE GENERAL

11
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:39,700
♪ and the streetlights keep on burning ♪

12
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,800
Dr. Hollis wants the intake forms
before rounds. All of them.

13
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,200
(SIGHS)

14
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:49,900
I mean, we both know she's going to
sign them without reading a single word.

15
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:51,000
Come on.

16
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:55,700
That's not the point and you know it.
Do it properly or don't do it at all.

17
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,400
Jesus, Marcus.

18
00:00:57,700 --> 00:01:01,200
You know what? Keep the moral high ground.
I'll keep the coffee.

19
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:03,900
<i>She was right, of course.</i>
<i>She usually was.</i>

20
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:07,600
NURSE (V.O.): Room four is asking
for you again, doctor.

21
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:09,300
Tell him I'm coming.

22
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,400
And that was the last quiet moment
any of us had for eleven hours.

23
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:20,100
Wait —

24
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:23,800
[MONITOR ALARM BLARING]
